            <ArticleTitle>A direct method for the N-tetraalkylation of azamacrocycles.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2457-2461</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3762/bjoc.12.239</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient protocol for the direct synthesis of N-tetraalkylated derivatives of the azamacrocycles cyclam and cyclen has been developed, using a partially miscible aqueous-organic solvent system with propargyl bromide, benzyl bromide, and related halides. The method works most effectively when the reaction mixture is shaken, not stirred. A crystal structure of the N-tetrapropargyl cyclam derivative 1,4,8,11-tetra(prop-2-yn-1-yl)-1,4,8,11-tetraazacyclotetradecane diperchlorate is reported.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
